o score in regulation time and extra time, after which Germany emerged victorious in the penalty shoot-out. Argentina and the Netherlands did score, twice each, and also had to decide the match by penalty shots. The Dutch won, making their first ever final (no final match was played in 1984, when they won the gold). With the 4-1 loss in the group stage, Germany was considered to be the underdog, but their adapted strategy worked out well. They optimally converted their goal opportunities in the first half, leading 2-0. The Dutch were the stronger team in the second half, but couldn’t come any closer than 2-1. The Germans became the fifth country to win the hockey gold since the event was introduced in 1980."] "\n"] [:button {:id "button567703", :class "btn btn-default"} "Details"] [:script {} "$('#button567703').click(splits)"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {}] [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Team"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {:data-toggle "tooltip", :data-placement "right", :data-original-title "Games Played", :class "split", :style "display: none"} "GP"] [:th {:style "display: none", :class "split"} "Goals"] [:th {:style "display: none", :class "split"} "Shots on Goal"] [:th {:style "display: none", :class "split"} "Field Goals"] [:th {:style "display: none", :class "split"} "Field Goal Attempts"] [:th {:style "display: none", :class "split"} "Penalty Corner Goals"] [:th {:style "display: none", :class "split"} "Penalty Corner Attempts"] [:th {:style "display: none", :class "split"} "Penalty Stroke Goals"] [:th {:style "display: none", :class "split"} "Penalty Stroke Attempts"] [:th {:style "display: none", :class "split"} "Green Cards"] [:th {:style "display: none", :class "split"} "Yellow Cards"] [:th {:style "display: none", :class "split"} "Red Cards"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {:class "accordion-toggle", :data-toggle "collapse", :data-target ".team-members-537017"} [:div {:clas